<p>
"Discrete or continuous?" is the wrong organizing question. The right one is how
$\nu$ sits relative to $\mu$: fully absolutely continuous, fully singular, or
somewhere in between. The same measure can look one way against
Lebesgue and a different way against counting measure or a Gaussian reference. The
next figure makes that change-of-base concrete.
</p>

